/**
 * Creates an {@link ArchiveInputStream} by automatically detecting the archive format from the provided input stream's signature.
 * This method reads a small portion of the input stream, attempts to match it against known archive signatures (ZIP, JAR, AR, CPIO, DUMP, TAR),
 * and then resets the stream to its original position before constructing the appropriate {@link ArchiveInputStream}.
 *
 * The detection order prioritizes formats with shorter, more distinct signatures (ZIP, JAR, AR, CPIO)
 * before attempting to detect formats requiring larger signature buffers (DUMP, TAR).
 * For TAR archives, an additional robust check is performed by attempting to parse the header to ensure it represents a valid TAR entry,
 * which helps to prevent misidentification of non-TAR files with similar byte sequences.
 *
 * The input stream must support {@link InputStream#mark(int)} and {@link InputStream#reset()} operations.
